<html>
<head><title>Plugins &amp; Other Software</title></head>
<body>
<h1>Plugins &amp; Other Software</h1>

<p class='note'>
	We haven’t played with all of these plugins, so don’t blame us if any
	of them eat your computer. Okay?
</p>

<h2>Applications</h2>

<dl class='appList'>
    <dt><a href='http://www.linphone.org'>LinPhone</a></dt>
    <dd>A <abbr title='Session Initiation Protocol'>SIP</abbr>-based
        <abbr title='Voice over IP'>VoIP</abbr>
        phone for <a href='http://www.gnome.org'>GNOME</a></dd>
    
    <dt><a href='http://www.openh323.org'>OpenH323</a></dt>
    <dd>An open-source H.323 stack</dd>
    
    <dt><a href='http://www.gnomemeeting.org'>GnomeMeeting</a></dt>
    <dd>An H.323 videoconferencing program</dd>

    <dt><a href='http://homepage.ntlworld.com/jfe1205/others.html'
        >Windows builds of Speex utilities</a></dt>
    <dd>Windows builds of speexenc, speexdec, and speexdrop</dd>

    <dt><a href='http://home.wanadoo.nl/~w.speek/speex.htm'
        >Speex Frontend</a></dt>
    <dd><a href='http://home.wanadoo.nl/~w.speek/'>Speek</a>
        (no relation to Speex) has written a frontend to
        speexenc and speexdec</dd>

    <dt><a href='http://www.jcraft.com/jroar/'>JRoar</a></dt>
    <dd>JRoar, a streaming
        server written entirely in Java, supports Speex in addition to
        <a href='http://www.vorbis.com/'>Ogg Vorbis</a></dd>
    
    <dt><a href='http://www.metadecks.org/software/sweep/'>Sweep</a></dt>
    <dd>Sweep
        is a full-featured digital audio editor for GNU/Linux, the BSDs, and
        compatible systems</dd>
    <dt><a href='http://www.asteriskpbx.org'>Asterisk</a></dt>
    <dd>
		Asterisk is an open-source
        <abbr title='private branch exchange'>PBX</abbr>
	</dd>
</dl>

<h2>Player Plugins &amp; Code Examples</h2>
<dl class='appList'>
    <dt><a href='http://www.saunalahti.fi/~cse/html/other.html'
        >Winamp and Cool Edit Plugins</a></dt>
    <dd>Written by Case</dd>
    <dt><a href='download/speex-xmms-nightly.tar.gz'>Speex XMMS plugin</a></dt>
    <dd>Written by Jens Burkal,
		&lt;<a href='mailto:jzb@rapanden.dk'>jzb@rapanden.dk</a>&gt;
		(Note: Although this file is hosted on this server, it’s our
		only copy of the plugin that we had around
		before jzb.rapanden.dk became inaccessible. No guarantees.)</dd>
	<dt>
		<a href='download/speexDS_setup.zip'>DirectShow filters</a>
		<a href='download/speexDS_source.zip'>(source)</a>
	</dt>
	<dd>Written by Jean-François Émond,
		&lt;<a href='mailto:emondjf@yahoo.com'>emondjf@yahoo.com</a>&gt;</dd>
	
	<dt><a href='download/Speex_Delphi_Demo.zip'>An Encoder written in Delphi</a></dt>
	<dd>Smallish Delphi example written by John Villar</dd>
    
</dl>
<h2>Other Implementations &amp; Language Bindings</h2>
<dl class='appList'>
	<dt><a href='download/jspeex.zip'>Jspeex</a></dt>
	<dd>
		written by Boyd Ebsworthy
		&lt;<a href='mailto:bebsworthy@entreview.com'>bebsworthy@entreview.com</a>&gt;
	</dd>
		
	<dt><a href='download/jspxdec.zip'>Java Implementation of Speex</a></dt>
	<dd>
		Written by James Lawrence
		&lt;<a href='mailto:james.lawrence@hellonetwork.com'
		>james.lawrence@hellonetwork.com</a>&gt;
		of
		<a href='http://www.hellonetwork.com'>hello Network</a>
	</dd>
	
	<dt><a href='download/PySpeex.tar.gz'>PySpeex</a></dt>
	<dd>Python bindings by David McNab</dd>
</dl>
